---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Notice — Aryze"
  description="How Aryze ApS handles personal data when you visit aryze.io or contact the company through this website."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy notice"
    lede="How Aryze ApS handles personal data when you visit this website or contact us."
  />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="muted"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 3 November 2026</p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Aryze ApS is the data controller for this website. Our company registration number is CVR 38895052 and our
        address is Bredgade 3, 2., 1260 Copenhagen K, Denmark. Questions about this notice or your personal data can be
        sent to <a href="mailto:info@aryze.io">info@aryze.io</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we process</h2>
      <p>
        The site does not use advertising cookies, tracking cookies or third-party analytics. The site is hosted on
        Vercel. Hosting and security services may process standard technical data, such as IP address, browser
        information, requested pages and timestamps, to deliver the site, maintain security and diagnose faults.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you contact us through a form on this site or by email, we process the information you provide, including
        your name, contact details, organisation and the content of your message. Please do not send confidential financial or identity documents
        through an initial website enquiry.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we process it</h2>
      <p>
        Technical data is processed where necessary for our legitimate interests in providing a secure and reliable
        website. Enquiry data is processed to respond to your request, take steps towards a potential business
        relationship, and keep appropriate business records. Where a legal obligation applies, we process the
        information needed to meet it.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and sharing</h2>
      <p>
        Technical logs are retained only as long as needed for delivery, security and fault investigation. Enquiry
        records are kept for as long as the discussion remains relevant and then deleted or archived in line with our
        legal and business-record obligations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Service providers supporting hosting, security and email may process this data. Website hosting is supplied by
        Vercel, the website forms are delivered to us by Formspree, and enquiry email is handled through Microsoft 365. We may also disclose data where required by law. If a
        provider processes data outside the European Economic Area, we use an applicable legal transfer mechanism and
        appropriate safeguards.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to the conditions in data-protection law, you may request access, correction, deletion or restriction of
        your personal data, object to processing based on legitimate interests, or request data portability. You may also
        lodge a complaint with the Danish Data Protection Agency (Datatilsynet) or the supervisory authority where you
        live or work.
      </p>
      <p>
        To exercise a right or ask a privacy question, email <a href="mailto:info@aryze.io">info@aryze.io</a>. We may
        need to verify your identity before acting on a request.
      </p>

      <h2>Scope of this notice</h2>
      <p>
        This notice covers this Aryze website and enquiries made through its forms and email links. Separate terms or privacy
        information may apply to a specific Aryze service, client engagement or regulated partner flow.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
